ty\"<|>\"生产技术改造项目\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Production Technology Renovation Project refers to engineering projects involving upgrades or improvements to power infrastructure, governed by specific settlement and accounting procedures.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"竣工决算\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Final Settlement refers to the comprehensive financial reconciliation process after project completion, covering all costs such as construction, equipment, labor, and management, conducted in accordance with contractual and regulatory requirements.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"竣工结算\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Final Settlement refers to the stage where project expenses are calculated and verified based on contracts, invoices, design changes, and other documentation following project completion.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"项目竣工验收\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Project Completion Acceptance is the formal inspection and confirmation that a project meets required standards and is ready for operational use.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"审计工作\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Audit Work involves reviewing final accounting reports to ensure accuracy, compliance, and proper financial reporting, typically conducted by internal or external auditors.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"账务调整\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Accounting Adjustment refers to the process of updating financial records based on approved final settlement decisions, usually completed within one month after receiving approval.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"转资手续\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Capital Transfer Procedures refer to the official process of transferring project costs into fixed asset accounts after final settlement approval.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"限上项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Limited-Upper Projects are defined as high-investment projects requiring individual compilation of settlement and final accounting reports, typically exceeding certain financial thresholds.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"限下项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Limited-Lower Projects are lower-value projects, with those having investments of 200 million yuan or more requiring individual rep