    "content": "(\"entity\"<|>\"国家电网公司\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"National Grid Corporation is a major power utility organization in China responsible for the management and operation of power systems. It has established standardized procedures for managing archival records related to production technology renovation and equipment overhaul projects. The company oversees various subsidiaries and regional units, ensuring compliance with national laws and internal regulations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网办公厅\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Office is the central administrative department responsible for overseeing project archival management across the company. It ensures compliance with national, industry, and corporate archival regulations, develops and maintains standards, and conducts supervision, guidance, inspection, evaluation, and assessment activities.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网运检部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Operation and Maintenance Department leads the management and coordination of project file archiving. It guides subordinate units, organizes the collection, sorting, and transfer of files from headquarters assets, and plays a key role in audit and quality control processes.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"财务部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Finance Department is responsible for providing financial documentation required for project archives and supporting the transfer of project-related files. It collaborates with project management departments to ensure accurate and timely archiving.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"审计部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Audit Department is responsible for supervising and verifying the accuracy and completeness of project-related documents during the archiving process. It supports the proper filing and transfer of project materials.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"物资部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Material Department manages the collection and organization of procurement-related documents including design, supervision, construction, and equipment (materials) bidding and contract files. It also verifies information such as bid award notices and procurement contracts.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"省（自治区、直辖市）电力公司\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Provincial Power Companies are regional subsidiaries of State Grid Corporation responsible for managing project archives within their jurisdictions. They implement company-wide policies and conduct oversight, inspection, and guidance on local archival practices.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网新源公司\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Xin Yuan Company is a directly affiliated unit under State Grid Corporation involved in energy infrastructure projects and subject to the same archival management requirements.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网运行公司\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Operation Company is a directly affiliated entity responsible for operational aspects of power systems and must comply with the company's project archival regulations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网信通公司\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Information & Communication Company is a directly affiliated unit focused on information and communication technologies, required to follow the same archival standards for its projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"地市公司级单位\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"City-level Companies are local operating units responsible for implementing archival policies at the grassroots level. They oversee document collection, verification, storage, utilization, and training activities.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"设计、监理、施工等参建单位\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Design, Supervision, and Construction Units are external contractors involved in project execution. They are responsible for collecting, organizing, and submitting project-related documentation in a timely manner, ensuring authenticity, accuracy, and completeness.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"项目档案\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Project Archives refer to all textual, graphical, audio-visual, and other materials generated throughout the entire lifecycle of production technology renovation and equipment overhaul projects, including pre-project planning, budgeting, implementation, and settlement stages. These documents must be preserved in both physical and digital formats.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"生产技术改造和设备大修项目\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Production Technology Renovation and Equipment Overhaul Projects are specific engineering initiatives managed by State Grid Corporation aimed at upgrading power system infrastructure. These projects span multiple phases and require strict adherence to archival standards.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"《中华人民共和国档案法》\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The Law of the People's Republic of China on Archives is a foundational legal framework that mandates proper archival practices and serves as a basis for internal regulations within State Grid Corporation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"DA/T28-2002\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Document Archive/Technical Requirements for Major National Construction Projects is a national standard specifying documentation and archive management procedures for large-scale construction projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"GB/T11822-2008\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"General Requirements for the Composition of Scientific and Technological Archives is a national standard defining the structure and content of technical archive volumes.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网（办/2）417-2014\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"State Grid Corporation’s Archive Management Measures (Document No. 417-2014) is an internal corporate regulation governing the management of archives within the company.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"GB/T 18894-2002\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Electronic Document Archiving and Management Standard is a national guideline for handling electronic records, requiring metadata preservation and long-term accessibility.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网（办/2）544-2014\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"State Grid Corporation’s Electronic Document Management Method (Document No. 544-2014) outlines rules for managing electronic files within the company.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Q/GDW 135-2006\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Technical Specifications for Digitization of Paper Archives by State Grid Corporation defines standards for converting paper documents into digital formats.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"一项目一档案\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"One Project, One Archive is a principle requiring that each project must have a single, complete, and uniquely identifiable set of archival records, ensuring traceability and integrity.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"分分别组卷，集中归档\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Separate Volume Formation, Centralized Archiving is a method used for backup packages in technical renovation projects, where individual sub-projects are grouped separately but archived centrally at the city-level company.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"自验收\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Self-inspection is the initial phase of archive quality assurance, conducted by the project management unit before formal submission. It involves reviewing the authenticity, accuracy, and completeness of archived materials and making necessary corrections.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"档案管理单位验收\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Archive Management Unit Inspection is the second stage of archival validation, carried out by operations and maintenance departments together with archive management departments to verify compliance with corporate standards.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"竣工投运后3个月内\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Within three months after project completion and commissioning is a deadline specified for completing the archival transfer of production technology renovation projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"竣工投运后1个月内\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Within one month after project completion and commissioning is a deadline for completing the archival transfer of equipment overhaul projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"2018年4月10日\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"April 10, 2018, is the effective date when this regulation came into force, marking the official implementation of the new archival management standards.\")##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网公司\"<|>\"国网办公厅\"<|>\"State Grid Office serves as the primary business management department for project archives within the company, responsible for 