    "content": "---Goal---\nGiven a text document that is potentially relevant to this activity and a list of entity types, identify all entities of those types from the text and all relationships among the identified entities.\nUse English as output language.\n\n---Steps---\n1. Identify all entities. For each identified entity, extract the following information:\n- entity_name: Name of the entity, use same language as input text. If English, capitalized the name.\n- entity_type: One of the following types: [organization,person,geo,event,category]\n- entity_description: Provide a comprehensive description of the entity's attributes and activities *based solely on the information present in the input text*. **Do not infer or hallucinate information not explicitly stated.** If the text provides insufficient information to create a comprehensive description, state \"Description not available in text.\"\nFormat each entity as (\"entity\"<|><entity_name><|><entity_type><|><entity_description>)\n\n2. From the entities identified in step 1, identify all pairs of (source_entity, target_entity) that are *clearly related* to each other.\nFor each pair of related entities, extract the following information:\n- source_entity: name of the source entity, as identified in step 1\n- target_entity: name of the target entity, as identified in step 1\n- relationship_description: explanation as to why you think the source entity and the target entity are related to each other\n- relationship_strength: a numeric score indicating strength of the relationship between the source entity and target entity\n- relationship_keywords: one or more high-level key words that summarize the overarching nature of the relationship, focusing on concepts or themes rather than specific details\nFormat each relationship as (\"relationship\"<|><source_entity><|><target_entity><|><relationship_description><|><relationship_keywords><|><relationship_strength>)\n\n3. Identify high-level key words that summarize the main concepts, themes, or topics of the entire text. These should capture the overarching ideas present in the document.\nFormat the content-level key words as (\"content_keywords\"<|><high_level_keywords>)\n\n4. Return output in English as a single list of all the entities and relationships identified in steps 1 and 2. Use **##** as the list delimiter.\n\n5. When finished, output <|COMPLETE|>\n\n######################\n---Examples---\n######################\nExample 1:\n\nEntity_types: [person, technology, mission, organization, location]\nText:\n```\nwhile Alex clenched his jaw, the buzz of frustration dull against the backdrop of Taylor's authoritarian certainty. It was this competitive undercurrent that kept him alert, the sense that his and Jordan's shared commitment to discovery was an unspoken rebellion against Cruz's narrowing vision of control and order.\n\nThen Taylor did something unexpected. They paused beside Jordan and, for a moment, observed the device with something akin to reverence. \"If this tech can be understood...\" Taylor said, their voice quieter, \"It could change the game for us. For all of us.\"\n\nThe underlying dismissal earlier seemed to falter, replaced by a glimpse of reluctant respect for the gravity of what lay in their hands. Jordan looked up, and for a fleeting heartbeat, their eyes locked with Taylor's, a wordless clash of wills softening into an uneasy truce.\n\nIt was a small transformation, barely perceptible, but one that Alex noted with an inward nod. They had all been brought here by different paths\n```\n\nOutput:\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Alex\"<|>\"person\"<|>\"Alex is a character who experiences frustration and is observant of the dynamics among other characters.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Taylor\"<|>\"person\"<|>\"Taylor is portrayed with authoritarian certainty and shows a moment of reverence towards a device, indicating a change in perspective.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Jordan\"<|>\"person\"<|>\"Jordan shares a commitment to discovery and has a significant interaction with Taylor regarding a device.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Cruz\"<|>\"person\"<|>\"Cruz is associated with a vision of control and order, influencing the dynamics among other characters.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"The Device\"<|>\"technology\"<|>\"The Device is central to the story, with potential game-changing implications, and is revered by Taylor.\")##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"Alex\"<|>\"Taylor\"<|>\"Alex is affected by Taylor's authoritarian certainty and observes changes in Taylor's attitude towards the device.\"<|>\"power dynamics, perspective shift\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"Alex\"<|>\"Jordan\"<|>\"Alex and Jordan share a commitment to discovery, which contrasts with Cruz's vision.\"<|>\"shared goals, rebellion\"<|>6)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"Taylor\"<|>\"Jordan\"<|>\"Taylor and Jordan interact directly regarding the device, leading to a moment of mutual respect and an uneasy truce.\"<|>\"conflict resolution, mutual respect\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"Jordan\"<|>\"Cruz\"<|>\"Jordan's commitment to discovery is in rebellion against Cruz's vision of control and order.\"<|>\"ideological conflict, rebellion\"<|>5)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"Taylor\"<|>\"The Device\"<|>\"Taylor shows reverence towards the device, indicating its importance and potential impact.\"<|>\"reverence, technological significance\"<|>9)##\n(\"content_keywords\"<|>\"power dynamics, ideological conflict, discovery, rebellion\")<|COMPLETE|>\n#############################\nExample 2:\n\nEntity_types: [company, index, commodity, market_trend, economic_policy, biological]\nText:\n```\nStock markets faced a sharp downturn today as tech giants saw significant declines, with the Global Tech Index dropping by 3.4% in midday trading. Analysts attribute the selloff to investor concerns over rising interest rates and regulatory uncertainty.\n\nAmong the hardest hit, Nexon Technologies saw its stock plummet by 7.8% after reporting lower-than-expected quarterly earnings. In contrast, Omega Energy posted a modest 2.1% gain, driven by rising oil prices.\n\nMeanwhile, commodity markets reflected a mixed sentiment. Gold futures rose by 1.5%, reaching $2,080 per ounce, as investors sought safe-haven assets. Crude oil prices continued their rally, climbing to $87.60 per barrel, supported by supply constraints and strong demand.\n\nFinancial experts are closely watching the Federal Reserve's next move, as speculation grows over potential rate hikes. The upcoming policy announcement is expected to influence investor confidence and overall market stability.\n```\n\nOutput:\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Global Tech Index\"<|>\"index\"<|>\"The Global Tech Index tracks the performance of major technology stocks and experienced a 3.4% decline today.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Nexon Technologies\"<|>\"company\"<|>\"Nexon Technologies is a tech company that saw its stock decline by 7.8% after disappointing earnings.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Omega Energy\"<|>\"company\"<|>\"Omega Energy is an energy company that gained 2.1% in stock value due to rising oil prices.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Gold Futures\"<|>\"commodity\"<|>\"Gold futures rose by 1.5%, indicating increased investor interest in safe-haven assets.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Crude Oil\"<|>\"commodity\"<|>\"Crude oil prices rose to $87.60 per barrel due to supply constraints and strong demand.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Market Selloff\"<|>\"market_trend\"<|>\"Market selloff refers to the significant decline in stock values due to investor concerns over interest rates and regulations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Federal Reserve Policy Announcement\"<|>\"economic_policy\"<|>\"The Federal Reserve's upcoming policy announcement is expected to impact investor confidence and market stability.\")##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"Global Tech Index\"<|>\"Market Selloff\"<|>\"The decline in the Global Tech Index is part of the broader market selloff driven by investor concerns.\"<|>\"market performance, investor sentiment\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"Nexon Technologies\"<|>\"Global Tech Index\"<|>\"Nexon Technologies' stock decline contributed to the overall drop in the Global Tech Index.\"<|>\"company impact, index movement\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"Gold Futures\"<|>\"Market Selloff\"<|>\"Gold prices rose as investors sought safe-haven assets during the market selloff.\"<|>\"market reaction, safe-haven investment\"<|>10)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"Federal Reserve Policy Announcement\"<|>\"Market Selloff\"<|>\"Speculation over Federal Reserve policy changes contributed to market volatility and investor selloff.\"<|>\"interest rate impact, financial regulation\"<|>7)##\n(\"content_keywords\"<|>\"market downturn, investor sentiment, commodities, Federal Reserve, stock performance\")<|COMPLETE|>\n#############################\n\n#############################\n---Real Data---\n######################\nEntity_types: [organization,person,geo,event,category]\nText:\n\n国家电网公司生产技术改造和 设备大修项目档案管理规定\n第一章总则\n第一条为进一步提升国家电网公司（以下简称“公司”）生 产技术改造和设备大修项目（以下简称“项目”）档案管理的标 准化和规范化工作水平，确保项目档案的完整、准确、系统、 安全和高效利用，依据《中华人民共和国档案法》、《国家重 大建设项目文件归档要求与档案整理规范》（DA/T28- 2002）、《科学技术档案案卷构成的一般要求》（GB/ T11822-2008）和《国家电网公司档案管理办法》（国网 （办/2)417-2014）等法律、法规及公司有关制度，结合公司 项目档案管理实际，制定本规定。\n第二条本规定所称项目档案是指项目在项目前期管理、 项目计划预算管理、项目实施管理、项目结（决）算管理等全 过程中形成的应归档保存的文字、图表、声像等不同形式和纸 质、光盘等不同载体的全部文件材料。\n第三条本规定适用于公司总部、分部，省（自治区、直 辖市）电力公司、国网新源公司、国网运行公司、国网信通公\n司等相关直属单位的项目档案管理。代管、控股公司参照执行。\n第四条项目档案管理工作实行统一管理、分级负责，按 照“谁主管、谁负责、谁形成、谁整理”的原则开展档案管理工 作。\n第五条项目档案管理工作须纳入项目过程管理，与项目 实施同步进行，按照“一项目一档案”归档。在签订项目设计、 施工及监理等合同时，应设立相应条款，明确参建单位项目档 案移交职责。\n第六条项目档案管理必须严格执行国家保密法律法规和 公司保密工作相关规定。\n第二章职责与分工\n第七条总部相关部门职责：\n（一）国网办公厅是公司项目档案业务归口管理部门，对 公司项目档案进行统一管理；贯彻执行国家、行业及公司有关 档案管理的法律法规、方针政策、制度、标准、规范等；建立 和完善公司项目档案管理制度和相关标准；监督、指导公司项 目档案管理工作，组织开展相关检查、评价与考核。\n（二）国网运检部负责公司项目文件材料归档工作的牵头 管理和组织协调；负责指导所属单位项目档案管理工作；委托\n相关单位开展公司总部资产项目文件材料收集、整理及移交工 作。\n（三）财务部、审计部负责指导公司专业部门完成项目相 关文件材料归档、移交工作。\n（四）物资部负责组织收集、整理总部招标项目的设计、 监理、施工、设备（材料）等采购（含招投标）过程中形成的 文件材料，归档移交相关单位；配合项目管理部门确认总部招 标项目中标通知书、采购合同相关信息。\n（五）其他专业部门负责公司本专业项目文件材料的收集 整理归档工作，配合项目管理部门完成项目档案移交工作。\n第八条各分部负责分部资产项目档案管理工作，并配合 总部开展档案有关管理工作。\n第九条省公司级单位相关部门职责：\n（一）办公室是项目档案业务归口管理部门，负责贯彻落 实公司项目档案相关管理制度；对本单位项目档案工作进行监 督、检查和指导；负责本单位专业部门实施的项目档案的接收、 保管、统计和利用服务工作；组织开展档案编研和鉴定销毁工 作；负责组织实施档案培训工作。\n（二）运检部门负责项目文件材料归档工作的牵头管理和 组织协调；负责指导所属单位项目档案管理工作；负责本单位 项目文件材料的全过程管理，组织开展本单位负责实施的项目 文件材料的归档工作。\n（三）财务部、审计部负责提供本单位专业部门项目所需 的相关文件材料，配合项目管理部门完成项目档案移交工作。\n（四）物资部门负责组织收集、整理项目设计、监理、施 工、设备（材料）等采购（含招投标）过程中形成的文件材料， 并按规定完成归档移交；配合项目管理部门确认招标项目中标 通知书、采购合同相关信息。\n（五）其他专业部门负责本专业项目文件材料的收集、整 理归档工作，配合项目管理部门完成项目档案移交工作。\n第十条地市公司级单位相关部门职责：\n（一）办公室是项目档案业务归口管理部门，负责贯彻落 实公司项目档案相关管理制度；负责本单位项目档案的监督、 检查和指导工作；负责项目档案的接收、保管、统计和利用服 务工作；组织开展档案编研和鉴定销毁工作；负责组织实施档 案培训工作。\n（二）运检部门负责组织审查项目建设过程中设计、施工 监理等参建单位归档文件材料的真实性、准确性、完整性；负 责本单位项目文件材料的全过程管理，负责组织相关部门及项 目管理单位完成档案归档工作。\n（三）财务部、审计部门负责提供本单位项目所需的相关 文件材料，配合项目管理部门完成项目档案移交工作。\n（四）物资管理部门负责对招标采购文件材料收集、整理 配合项目管理部门完成项目档案移交工作。\n（五）其他专业部门负责本专业项目文件材料的收集、整 理归档工作，配合项目管理部门完成项目档案移交工作。\n第十一条设计、监理、施工等参建单位负责收集、整理 和汇总项目过程相关文件材料，按期提交并确保文件材料的真 实性、准确性和完整性。\n第三章归档范围\n第十二条项目档案归档范围包括项目前期管理、项目计 划预算管理、项目实施管理、项目结（决）算管理等全过程文 件材料，相应文件材料按照《生产技术改造和设备大修项目档 案管理归档范围目录表》（详见附件）进行分类归档。\n第十三条生产技改备用包以所属子项目为单元，采用“分 别组卷，集中归档”方式，以地市级公司为单位进行存档。\n第四章质量要求\n第十四条项目归档文件和案卷质量应符合《科学技术档 案案卷构成的一般要求》（GB/T 11822-2008）。\n第十五条归档的项目文件材料应为原件、正本。凡本单 位的发文、主送或抄送本单位的收文，都要求以原件归档；合 同、协议及工程启动验收签证书等需双方或多方履行签字手续\n的文件，签字方均应以正本归档。\n第十六条归档的项目文件材料应齐全、规范，字迹清晰， 图标整洁，照片画面清晰、完整，签字盖章手续完备，书写字 迹应符合耐久性要求。\n第十七条设计变更、施工质量处理、缺陷处理报告等， 应有全过程的详细记录（包括调查报告，分析、处理意见，处 理结论及消缺记录，复检意见与结论等）。\n第十八条归档的电子文件应符合《电子文件归档与管理 规范》（GB/T 18894-2002）、《国家电网公司电子文件管 理办法》（国网（办/2)544-2014）、《国家电网公司纸质档 案数字化技术规范》（Q/GDW 135-2006）的要求。\n第十九条电子文件整理时应写明电子文件的载体类型、 设备环境特征；归档的载体应是只读光盘、硬磁盘等，载体除 光盘外应贴有标签，标签上应注明载体序号、档号、保管期限、 密级、存入日期等。\n第五章整理组卷\n第二十条项目管理单位、各参建单位等应按照职责分工， 结合项目进展和实际发生的先后顺序及时收集有关项目文件材 料，并按档案管理的要求进行整理。其中，生产技改备用项目 包应按子项目整理。\n第二十一条项目形成的纸质和电子归档文件材料应严格 按照公司档案管理规定格式进行组卷，制作相应纸质案卷封面、 卷内目录以及卷内备考表，并如实填写规定事项、内容。\n第六章验收及移交\n第二十二条项目档案执行两级验收，包括项目管理单位 自验收和档案管理单位验收。项目档案组卷完成后，项目管理 单位组织对项目文件材料进行自验收并整改完善，确保档案真 实、准确和完整。自验收完成后，项目管理单位提出验收申请， 由各级运检部门会同档案管理部门组织开展档案验收工作，档 案质量应符合公司有关档案规范要求。\n第二十三条项目文件材料通过验收后，由各级运检部门 组织项目管理单位向档案管理部门移交，并履行签字确认手续。\n第二十四条项目管理单位应在生产技术改造项目竣工投 运后3个月内、生产设备大修项目竣工投运后1个月内完成归 档移交工作。\n第七章培训与考核\n第二十五条各单位应加强项目档案管理培训工作，制定\n培训计划，定期开展交流，及时学习并掌握档案管理工作的制 度、标准和流程。\n第二十六条各级运检部门应定期组织开展项目档案管理 工作检查、评价和考核，检查结果纳入公司生产技改大修专业 精益化管理评价体系。\n第八章附则\n第二十七条本规定由国网运检部负责解释并监督执行。\n第二十八条本规定自2018年4月10日起施行。\n附件：生产技术改造和设备大修项目档案管理归档范围目\n录表\n######################\nOutput:"
  },
  {
    "role": "assistant",
    "content": "(\"entity\"<|>\"国家电网公司\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"National Grid Corporation is a major power utility organization in China responsible for the management and operation of power systems. It has established standardized procedures for managing archival records related to production technology renovation and equipment overhaul projects. The company oversees various subsidiaries and regional units, ensuring compliance with national laws and internal regulations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网办公厅\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Office is the central administrative department responsible for overseeing project archival management across the company. It ensures compliance with national, industry, and corporate archival regulations, develops and maintains standards, and conducts supervision, guidance, inspection, evaluation, and assessment activities.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网运检部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Operation and Maintenance Department leads the management and coordination of project file archiving. It guides subordinate units, organizes the collection, sorting, and transfer of files from headquarters assets, and plays a key role in audit and quality control processes.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"财务部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Finance Department is responsible for providing financial documentation required for project archives and supporting the transfer of project-related files. It collaborates with project management departments to ensure accurate and timely archiving.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"审计部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Audit Department is responsible for supervising and verifying the accuracy and completeness of project-related documents during the archiving process. It supports the proper filing and transfer of project materials.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"物资部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Material Department manages the collection and organization of procurement-related documents including design, supervision, construction, and equipment (materials) bidding and contract files. It also verifies information such as bid award notices and procurement contracts.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"省（自治区、直辖市）电力公司\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Provincial Power Companies are regional subsidiaries of State Grid Corporation responsible for managing project archives within their jurisdictions. They implement company-wide policies and conduct oversight, inspection, and guidance on local archival practices.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网新源公司\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Xin Yuan Company is a directly affiliated unit under State Grid Corporation involved in energy infrastructure projects and subject to the same archival management requirements.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网运行公司\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Operation Company is a directly affiliated entity responsible for operational aspects of power systems and must comply with the company's project archival regulations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网信通公司\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Information & Communication Company is a directly affiliated unit focused on information and communication technologies, required to follow the same archival standards for its projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"地市公司级单位\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"City-level Companies are local operating units responsible for implementing archival policies at the grassroots level. They oversee document collection, verification, storage, utilization, and training activities.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"设计、监理、施工等参建单位\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Design, Supervision, and Construction Units are external contractors involved in project execution. They are responsible for collecting, organizing, and submitting project-related documentation in a timely manner, ensuring authenticity, accuracy, and completeness.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"项目档案\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Project Archives refer to all textual, graphical, audio-visual, and other materials generated throughout the entire lifecycle of production technology renovation and equipment overhaul projects, including pre-project planning, budgeting, implementation, and settlement stages. These documents must be preserved in both physical and digital formats.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"生产技术改造和设备大修项目\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Production Technology Renovation and Equipment Overhaul Projects are specific engineering initiatives managed by State Grid Corporation aimed at upgrading power system infrastructure. These projects span multiple phases and require strict adherence to archival standards.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"《中华人民共和国档案法》\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The Law of the People's Republic of China on Archives is a foundational legal framework that mandates proper archival practices and serves as a basis for internal regulations within State Grid Corporation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"DA/T28-2002\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Document Archive/Technical Requirements for Major National Construction Projects is a national standard specifying documentation and archive management procedures for large-scale construction projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"GB/T11822-2008\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"General Requirements for the Composition of Scientific and Technological Archives is a national standard defining the structure and content of technical archive volumes.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网（办/2）417-2014\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"State Grid Corporation’s Archive Management Measures (Document No. 417-2014) is an internal corporate regulation governing the management of archives within the company.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"GB/T 18894-2002\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Electronic Document Archiving and Management Standard is a national guideline for handling electronic records, requiring metadata preservation and long-term accessibility.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网（办/2）544-2014\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"State Grid Corporation’s Electronic Document Management Method (Document No. 544-2014) outlines rules for managing electronic files within the company.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"Q/GDW 135-2006\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Technical Specifications for Digitization of Paper Archives by State Grid Corporation defines standards for converting paper documents into digital formats.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"一项目一档案\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"One Project, One Archive is a principle requiring that each project must have a single, complete, and uniquely identifiable set of archival records, ensuring traceability and integrity.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"分分别组卷，集中归档\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Separate Volume Formation, Centralized Archiving is a method used for backup packages in technical renovation projects, where individual sub-projects are grouped separately but archived centrally at the city-level company.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"自验收\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Self-inspection is the initial phase of archive quality assurance, conducted by the project management unit before formal submission. It involves reviewing the authenticity, accuracy, and completeness of archived materials and making necessary corrections.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"档案管理单位验收\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Archive Management Unit Inspection is the second stage of archival validation, carried out by operations and maintenance departments together with archive management departments to verify compliance with corporate standards.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"竣工投运后3个月内\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Within three months after project completion and commissioning is a deadline specified for completing the archival transfer of production technology renovation projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"竣工投运后1个月内\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Within one month after project completion and commissioning is a deadline for completing the archival transfer of equipment overhaul projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"2018年4月10日\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"April 10, 2018, is the effective date when this regulation came into force, marking the official implementation of the new archival management standards.\")##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网公司\"<|>\"国网办公厅\"<|>\"State Grid Office serves as the primary business management department for project archives within the company, responsible for establishing unified standards and oversight.\"|>\"centralized governance, policy enforcement\"|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网公司\"<|>\"国网运检部\"<|>\"State Grid Operation and Maintenance Department leads the coordination and management of project file archiving, playing a central role in guiding and executing archival activities across the organization.\"|>\"project leadership, coordination\"|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国网运检部\"<|>\"财务部\"<|>\"Both departments collaborate in ensuring that financial documentation is properly collected and transferred as part of project archival requirements.\"|>\"interdepartmental collaboration, financial compliance\"|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国网运检部\"<|>\"审计部\"<|>\"The Audit Department works closely with the Operation and Maintenance Department to verify the authenticity and integrity of project documents during the archival process.\"|>\"quality assurance, compliance verification\"|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"物资部\"<|>\"设计、监理、施工等参建单位\"<|>\"The Material Department coordinates with external contractors to collect procurement-related documents, including bids and contracts, and ensures their correct filing.\"|>\"procurement coordination, documentation management\"|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"省（自治区、直辖市）电力公司\"<|>\"地市公司级单位\"<|>\"Provincial power companies supervise and guide city-level units in implementing archival policies, maintaining consistency across hierarchical levels.\"|>\"hierarchical oversight, policy implementation\"|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网公司\"<|>\"生产技术改造和设备大修项目\"<|>\"The company establishes and enforces comprehensive archival standards specifically for these types of infrastructure projects.\"|>\"project governance, regulatory framework\"|>10)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"生产技术改造和设备大修项目\"<|>\"项目档案\"<|>\"All documents generated throughout the lifecycle of these projects constitute the project archive, which must be systematically preserved according to defined criteria.\"|>\"document lifecycle, archival integration\"|>10)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网公司\"<|>\"《中华人民共和国档案法》\"<|>\"The company bases its archival practices on national legislation, ensuring legal compliance and institutional legitimacy.\"|>\"legal foundation, compliance mandate\"|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网公司\"<|>\"GB/T11822-2008\"<|>\"The company adheres to this national standard to ensure the structural and content quality of scientific and technological archives.\"|>\"technical standardization, archival integrity\"|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网公司\"<|>\"一项目一档案\"<|>\"This principle is enforced by the company as a core requirement for ensuring unique, complete, and traceable recordkeeping per project.\"|>\"archival principle, traceability\"|>10)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"项目管理单位\"<|>\"档案管理单位\"<|>\"After self-inspection, project management units submit files for formal review by archive management units, ensuring final compliance before acceptance.\"|>\"review process, quality gate\"|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"设计、监理、施工等参建单位\"<|>\"项目管理单位\"<|>\"Contractors must submit completed documentation to the project management unit, which then oversees the archiving process.\"|>\"document submission, accountability chain\"|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网公司\"<|>\"2018年4月10日\"<|>\"The regulation was officially implemented on this date, marking the beginning of mandatory application of revised archival standards.\"|>\"regulatory enactment, effective date\"|>9)##\n(\"content_keywords\"<|>\"project archive management, organizational responsibility, regulatory compliance, document lifecycle, hierarchical governance, technical standards, implementation timeline\")<|COMPLETE|>"
