    "content": "(\"entity\"<|>\"国家电网有限公司\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"National Grid Corporation Limited is a major state-owned enterprise responsible for managing and operating the power grid infrastructure in China. It establishes regulations and standards for the maintenance and repair of grid equipment, ensuring safety, reliability, and economic operation of the power system.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网设备部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Equipment Department is the primary management department responsible for overseeing power grid production equipment overhaul work across the company. It enforces national and industry policies, develops regulations and technical standards, manages project planning and budgeting, and supervises project implementation and evaluation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网发展部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Development Department is the centralized management department for comprehensive planning within the company. It integrates power grid production equipment overhaul plans into the company’s overall planning framework.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网财务部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Finance Department is the central authority for budget management. It ensures that funds allocated for equipment overhaul are incorporated into the company's unified budget system.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网办公室\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Office is the central department responsible for archival management. It supervises, guides, evaluates, and conducts acceptance of project archives, particularly for headquarters-funded projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网审计部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Audit Department oversees audit activities for headquarters-funded projects and provides guidance to divisions and subsidiaries on project auditing.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网物资部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Material Department manages procurement activities within the headquarters' centralized procurement scope and supports project management across departments.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国调中心\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Dispatching Center is responsible for formulating professional principles related to equipment overhaul, guiding implementation across divisions and units, and managing direct operation and maintenance assets.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"分部安质部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Division Safety and Quality Department manages equipment overhaul projects funded by the division. It collaborates with headquarters on reviews and evaluations and supervises regional overhaul activities.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"分部规划统计部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Division Planning and Statistics Department integrates the division’s equipment overhaul plans into the division’s comprehensive planning system.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"分部财务部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Division Finance Department manages the budgeting of equipment overhaul funds at the division level, integrating them into the division’s unified budget.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"区域审计中心\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Regional Audit Center conducts audits for projects funded by the division and supports compliance and financial oversight.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"调控分中心\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Dispatching Sub-center manages professional project work and oversees the reserve, planning, and execution of directly operated asset projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"各单位设备管理部门\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Each unit’s Equipment Management Department serves as the primary manager for local equipment overhaul work. It implements national and company policies, maintains project reserves, approves feasibility studies, and oversees project execution.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"各单位发展部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Each unit’s Development Department integrates local equipment overhaul plans into the unit’s comprehensive planning process.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"各单位财务部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Each unit’s Finance Department manages the budgeting of local equipment overhaul funds, incorporating them into the unit’s unified budget.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"各单位办公室\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Each unit’s Office supervises, guides, evaluates, and conducts acceptance of project archive management within the unit.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"各单位物资部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Each unit’s Material Department organizes procurement activities within its centralized procurement scope and manages disposal of old materials from projects; it also supports headquarters-level procurement and performs professional project management.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"各单位审计部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Each unit’s Audit Department conducts internal audits of implemented projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"调控中心\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Dispatching Center manages professional project work and handles the reserve, planning, and execution of directly operated asset projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"地市级公司设备管理部门\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"City-level Company Equipment Management Department is responsible for managing the reserve, planning, and implementation of operational asset projects within the city and conducting supervision and inspection.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网经研院\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Economic Research Institute conducts feasibility reviews for limit-up projects and preliminary design reviews for headquarters-operated assets. Provincial and municipal economic research institutes conduct similar reviews under commission.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"限上项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Limit-up projects refer to those with single investment of 15 million yuan or more, headquarters-funded projects, inter-provincial entrusted operation and maintenance assets, or other major projects designated by headquarters.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"限下项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Limit-down projects include all projects not classified as limit-up projects, covering smaller-scale investments and routine maintenance activities.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"应急项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Emergency projects are those urgently required due to natural disasters, force majeure, equipment damage, or critical defects, necessitating immediate implementation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"公司指定加快实施项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Company-designated fast-track projects are those requiring accelerated implementation following decision-making procedures due to changes in policy, environment, or technology.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电网生产设备大修\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Grid production equipment overhaul refers to repair work conducted to restore assets such as equipment, facilities, and auxiliary structures to their original condition and functionality. It does not increase fixed asset value and is treated as an expense rather than an investment.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"项目可研\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Project feasibility study (or project proposal) is a document prepared to assess the technical, economic, and operational viability of an overhaul project. It includes cost estimates and must meet specific depth requirements for bidding and procurement.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"项目储备库\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Project reserve database is a continuously maintained pool of potential overhaul projects derived from demand assessments. Projects are added after feasibility review and ranked based on urgency and importance.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"总部\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"Headquarters refers to the central management office of State Grid Corporation Limited, located in Beijing, which oversees corporate-wide policies, budgets, and strategic direction.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"分部\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"Division refers to regional administrative units under State Grid Corporation Limited, responsible for managing operations and projects within their respective geographic areas.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"省（自治区、直辖市）电力公司\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"Provincial (autonomous region, municipality) power companies are regional subsidiaries of State Grid Corporation Limited, responsible for power grid operations and equipment maintenance within their jurisdictions.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"全球能源互联网集团\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Global Energy Internet Group is a subsidiary of State Grid Corporation Limited involved in energy internet initiatives and infrastructure development.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网直流中心\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid DC Center specializes in the operation and maintenance of high-voltage direct current transmission systems.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网信通公司\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Information and Communication Company manages information and communication systems supporting grid operations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网经研院\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Economic Research Institute is a think tank providing technical and economic analysis for major grid projects.\")##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网有限公司\"<|>\"国网设备部\"<|>\"The State Grid Equipment Department is the primary management department responsible for overseeing equipment overhaul activities under the authority of National Grid Corporation Limited.\"<|>\"organizational hierarchy, regulatory oversight\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网有限公司\"<|>\"国网发展部\"<|>\"The State Grid Development Department integrates equipment overhaul plans into the company’s comprehensive planning system, ensuring alignment with strategic goals.\"<|>\"planning integration, organizational coordination\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网有限公司\"<|>\"国网财务部\"<|>\"The State Grid Finance Department manages the budgeting of overhaul funds, ensuring financial control and transparency across all levels.\"<|>\"budgetary control, financial governance\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网有限公司\"<|>\"国网办公室\"<|>\"The State Grid Office oversees archival management for projects, ensuring documentation integrity and compliance.\"<|>\"document management, compliance oversight\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网有限公司\"<|>\"国网审计部\"<|>\"The State Grid Audit Department conducts audits on headquarters-funded projects, ensuring accountability and risk mitigation.\"<|>\"financial audit, compliance monitoring\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网有限公司\"<|>\"国网物资部\"<|>\"The State Grid Material Department manages procurement 