ategic need, outlining conditions for each type.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"第九条\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Article Nine assigns the State Grid Equipment Department as the central management body responsible for enforcing policies, developing standards, approving limit-up projects, and supervising implementation across the organization.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"第十条\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Article Ten details the functional responsibilities of various headquarters departments, including planning, finance, archives, audit, and procurement, in supporting the oversight and integration of overhaul activities.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"第十一条\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Article Eleven outlines the role of Division Safety and Quality Departments in managing division-funded projects, conducting reviews, and supervising regional implementation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"第十二条\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Article Twelve specifies the responsibilities of division-level departments such as planning, finance, office, audit center, and professional management bodies in integrating and managing local overhaul projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"第十三条\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Article Thirteen assigns local unit equipment departments as the primary managers for overhaul work within their jurisdictions, responsible for feasibility review, planning, budgeting, and execution oversight.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"第十四条\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Article Fourteen details the support functions of local unit departments—development, finance, office, material, audit, and dispatching centers—in aligning plans, budgets, audits, procurement, and project execution.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"第十五条\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Article Fifteen designates city-level equipment departments as responsible for managing operational asset projects, including reserve, planning, implementation, and supervision.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"第十六条\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Article Sixteen assigns the State Grid Economic Research Institute and provincial/local research institutes the task of reviewing feasibility studies 