    "content": "(\"entity\"<|>\"国家电网公司西南分部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The State Grid Corporation of China Southwest Branch is a regional division responsible for managing power grid production technology renovation and equipment major repair projects within its jurisdiction. It oversees both directly operated and entrusted assets, ensuring compliance with national and corporate standards.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国家电网有限公司\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Corporation of China is the parent organization that establishes policies, regulations, and standards governing power grid production technology renovation and equipment major repair activities. It issues key documents such as the 'Management Regulations for Power Grid Production Technology Renovation Work' and 'Management Regulations for Power Grid Equipment Major Repair Work.'\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"生产技术部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The Production Technology Department is the primary management department within the State Grid Corporation of China Southwest Branch responsible for overseeing all aspects of power grid production technology renovation and equipment major repair work, including planning, project feasibility studies, budgeting, implementation monitoring, and post-evaluation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"发展规划部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The Planning and Development Department is the designated department responsible for integrating power grid production technology renovation plans and project schedules into the overall planning and comprehensive plan of the Southwest Branch. It leads project feasibility reviews, approves non-limit projects, and manages the project reserve database.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"财务资产部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The Finance and Asset Department manages the budgeting and financial control of power grid production technology renovation and equipment major repair projects. It ensures funds are included in the unified budget, handles project settlement and capitalization, and supports audit and evaluation processes.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"办公室\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The Office serves as the central authority for archival management within the Southwest Branch, supervising, guiding, inspecting, and evaluating project documentation across all departments and units.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"西南审计中心\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The Southwest Audit Center conducts final settlement audits for direct-operation asset projects and performs management audits on entrusted operation assets, ensuring financial and procedural compliance.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"安全监察部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The Safety Supervision Department oversees the safety, quality, and progress of project implementation, and assists in identifying emergency projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"调度控制中心\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The Dispatch Control Center manages professional project operations, coordinates power outage plans, and participates in project planning, preparation, and implementation for directly operated assets.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"受托运维省公司\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The provincial company entrusted with operation and maintenance acts as the management unit for projects involving assets under its operational responsibility. It integrates these projects into its own management system and implements related technical renovations and repairs.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"省公司所属超高压公司\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The Extra-high Voltage Company under the provincial company is the specific executing unit responsible for carrying out technology renovation and major repair projects on entrusted assets. It manages planning, reserves, implementation, procurement, settlement, auditing, and safety integration.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"限上项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A category of projects defined by investment thresholds: those with single investments of 20 million yuan or more for primary grid technology renovation, 15 million yuan or more for secondary system renovation, or total costs of 15 million yuan or more for equipment major repairs.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"限下项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Projects that do not meet the criteria for 'limit-up' projects; they include all other technology renovation and major repair projects not classified as limit-up.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"常规项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Standard projects that follow regular planning, approval, and execution procedures without urgency or special designation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"应急项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Projects initiated urgently due to natural disasters, force majeure, equipment damage, or critical defects requiring immediate action.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"公司指定加快实施项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Projects that must be expedited due to changes in policy, environment, or technology, following formal decision-making procedures.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电网生产技术改造\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"A process involving the use of mature, advanced, and applicable technologies, equipment, processes, and materials to upgrade existing power grid production assets, enhancing safety, reliability, economy, and alignment with intelligent, energy-saving, and environmental goals. This activity results in fixed asset formation and represents capital expenditure.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电网生产设备大修\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"A repair-based activity aimed at restoring the original condition and functionality of power grid assets (including equipment, facilities, and auxiliary systems) through project-based management. It does not increase fixed asset value and is considered an expense-driven, revenue-impacting expenditure.\")##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网公司西南分部\"<|>\"生产技术部\"<|>\"The Production Technology Department is the designated functional department responsible for managing all aspects of technology renovation and equipment major repair activities within the Southwest Branch.\" <|>\"organizational hierarchy, management responsibility\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网公司西南分部\"<|>\"发展规划部\"<|>\"The Planning and Development Department integrates the Southwest Branch’s technology renovation and repai