    "content": "(\"entity\"<|>\"公司总部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Company headquarters is responsible for making decisions on the annual plan and budget, including issuing details of projects above a certain threshold and overseeing adjustments to project plans and budgets.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"分部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Divisions are responsible for managing projects below a certain threshold, including decomposing investment scales and submitting project plan proposals to headquarters.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"各单位\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Units refer to individual operational entities under the company that manage their own limited project investments and must follow internal decision-making procedures before implementing changes.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国网设备部\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"State Grid Equipment Department is responsible for initiating preparatory work for pre-arranged projects based on the company's annual planning requirements.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"项目储备库\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Project reserve database is a repository from which all project plans must originate before being included in the annual plan or pre-arranged schedule.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"可研批复\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Feasibility study approval refers to the official endorsement required before any project can be included in the annual plan or pre-arranged schedule.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"预安排限上项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Pre-arranged projects above a certain scale are those that require centralized approval and management by headquarters.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"限下项目投入规模\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Limited project investment scale refers to the total funding allocation available to divisions and units for projects below a specified threshold.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"项目里程碑计划\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Project milestone plan is a timeline developed after project approval to guide implementation and control progress.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"招投标管理规定\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Bidding and tendering management regulations are rules requiring that all projects must be subject to bidding when applicable, ensuring transparency and compliance.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"初步设计\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Preliminary design is a phase required for projects exceeding 100 million yuan or involving significant design changes, with strict review and approval processes.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"施工图设计\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Construction drawing design is a mandatory step following preliminary design, based on approved documents and used for actual construction.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"竣工图\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Final drawings are updated versions of construction drawings incorporating all design changes and as-built conditions.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"设计变更\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Design changes occur during implementation and require formal documentation, including cost impact, justification, and approvals.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"项目监理\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Project supervision is required for non-self-implemented projects meeting specific criteria, such as size, complexity, or safety risk.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"项目竣工验收\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Project completion acceptance is conducted according to national standards, design documents, and supervisory reports, with responsibilities divided between entrusted and commissioning parties.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"项目结算\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Project settlement involves reviewing costs from design, construction, and other parties and preparing a report within 45 days of acceptance.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"拆旧管理\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Demolition and disposal management includes listing materials to be removed during project execution and transferring them to material departments for handling.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"档案管理\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Archival management follows the principle of 'who forms, who manages' and requires full documentation to be archived within two months of project completion.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"应急项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Emergency projects are initiated in response to sudden events like grid ac