ed units centrally procure equipment and materials, which are then delivered directly to the project site.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"基本预备费\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A reserve fund included in project costs to cover unforeseen expenses, though it is generally not applied in most grid technology renovation and equipment overhaul projects.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"特殊项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A category referring to cost items that are not covered by standard project divisions, existing quotas, or fee structures but are necessary for actual implementation, such as transition measures.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"应急改造工程项目\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"A type of urgent project involving infrastructure upgrades under emergency conditions, with a cost structure excluding basic contingency funds and including special emergency-related fees.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"应急抢修工程项目\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"A rapid response project for repairing damaged grid components, characterized by no inclusion of basic contingency funds and specific cost allocations for emergency mobilization and safety measures.\")##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"《电网技术改造及检修工程定额和费用计算规定 （2020年版）》\"<|>\"国家电网有限公司\"<|>\"The document was established and implemented by State Grid Corporation of China to guide standardized cost estimation practices across its operations.\" <|>\"regulatory framework, organizational policy\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网有限公司\"<|>\"附件1\"<|>\"The organization created and provided the comparative analysis in Attachment 1 to support understanding of changes between the 2015 and 2020 editions of the regulations.\" <|>\"document creation, policy update\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网有限公司\"<|>\"附件2\"<|>\"The organization developed Attachment 2 to specify the hierarchical application of engineering quotas, ensuring consistency in project estimation practices.\" <|>\"standardization, procedural guidance\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家电网有限公司\"<|>\"附件3\"<|>\"The organization authored Attachment 3 to detail the structure and content requirements for estimation books, ensuring uniformity across projects.\" <|>\"documentation, procedural compliance\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"概算定额\"<|>\"预算定额\"<|>\"The two types of quotas are sequentially applied depending on project maturity: estimate quotas are used early in the process, while budget quotas apply later or in more detailed phases.\" <|>\"quota hierarchy, project lifecycle\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"设备材料信息价\"<|>\"甲供方式\"<|>\"When equipment and materials are procured through centralized procurement (i.e., 'supplier delivery'), their prices are referenced from the company’s internal information price database.\" <|>\"procurement method, pricing reference\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"特殊项目\"<|>\"基本预备费\"<|>\"Special projects do not include basic contingency funds, indicating a deliberate exclusion of this cost component due to unique project nature.\" <|>\"cost structure, exception handling\"<|>6)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"应急改造工程项目\"<|>\"应急抢修工程项目\"<|>\"Both are emergency-based project types with similar cost features—excluding basic contingency funds and incorporating emergency-specific fees—but differ in scope and duration.\" <|>\"emergency projects, cost differentiation\"<|>7)##\n(\"content_keywords\"<|>\"grid technical renovation, equipment overhaul, cost estimation, engineering quotas, procurement standards, emergency projects\")<|COMPLETE|>"
