ss of modifying project schedules and funding allocations due to changed conditions, governed by strict procedures.\"|>##  \n(\"entity\"<|>\"管理权限\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Management authority refers to the level of decision-making power delegated to different organizational units, determining who can approve or modify projects.\"|>##  \n(\"entity\"<|>\"资金重大调整\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Major financial adjustment refers to significant changes in project costs that require re-evaluation of feasibility and formal approval processes.\"|>##  \n(\"entity\"<|>\"招标采购因素\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Bidding and procurement factors refer to variables arising from tendering processes that may influence project investment, requiring procedural updates if changes exceed thresholds.\"|>##  \n(\"entity\"<|>\"设备技术鉴定及处置意见\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Equipment technical appraisal and disposal opinion is a document required in feasibility studies that evaluates the condition and recommended action (e.g., repair, replacement) for decommissioned equipment.\"|>##  \n(\"entity\"<|>\"拟拆除设备\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Equipment slated for removal refers to assets identified for decommissioning, whose technical status and disposal plans must be documented in project proposals.\"|>##  \n(\"entity\"<|>\"公司总部下达总控目标\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"The company headquarters issues overarching targets for total project investment, which serve as the foundation for division-level planning and budget formulation.\"|>##  \n(\"entity\"<|>\"分部决策程序\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Division decision-making procedure refers to internal governance processes at the division level for approving projects, adjustments, and budget allocations.\"|>##  \n(\"entity\"<|>\"统一履行分部决策程序\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Unified execution of division decision-making process refers to the coordinated effort across departments (e.g., Planning, Finance) to approve projects or changes at the division level.\"|>##  \n(\"entity\"<|>\"重新履行可研审批程序\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Re-performing the feasibility study approval process is required when significant changes occur in project scope or cost, ensuring updated validation.\"|>##  \n(\"entity\"<|>\"计划建议组成项目\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Project components included in the plan proposal must originate from the project reserve library and be approved prior to inclusion in annual plans.\"|>##  \n(\"entity\"<|>\"项目时效性\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Project timeliness refers to the urgency of project execution, especially in relation to seasonal demand or infrastructure vulnerability, influencing priority and scheduling.\"|>##  \n(\"entity\"<|>\"轻重缓急\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Urgency ranking based on importance, severity, and immediacy is used to prioritize projects within the reserve library, ensuring efficient resource allocation.\"|>##  \n(\"entity\"<|>\"评审意见出具时间超过3年\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"A project with a feasibility review opinion older than three years must be removed from the reserve library unless it is re-validated through the full entry process.\"|>##  \n(\"entity\"<|>\"项目前期发生的可行性研究等费用支出\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Costs incurred during project pre-phase activities, such as feasibility studies, may be included in the annual budget for proper financial tracking and allocation.\"|>##  \n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家\"<|>\"项目调整\"<|>\"Changes in national policy may necessitate the adjustment, suspension, or termination of equipment technology renovation and major overhaul projects.\"|>\"policy impact, project modification\"|>9)##  \n(\"relationship\"<|>\"地方\"<|>\"项目调整\"<|>\"Local policy shifts can also trigger project adjustments, particularly in the context of regulatory or environmental requirements affecting project feasibility.\"|>\"regulatory change, local governance\"|>8)##  \n(\"relationship\"<|>\"公司总部\"<|>\"限上项目\"<|>\"The Company Headquarters is responsible for reviewing and approving limit-up projects after initial assessment by the Division and Production Technology Department.\"|>\"central oversight, approval authority\"|>10)##  \n(\"relationship\"